# Leak-guard denylist (template) — copy to `.leakcheck`, which is gitignored.
#
# internal/leakcheck scans the tracked tree for these tokens (case-insensitive, literal) and
# fails the build if any appears. Kube context/cluster/namespace names and cloud account IDs are
# derived automatically from your kubeconfig — list here only what a kubeconfig can't surface:
# internal PRODUCT and SERVICE names that show up in dogfooding notes (a real workload name, an
# internal middleware, a private cluster nickname).
#
# One token per line; '#' starts a comment. Keep this .example free of any real name.
#
# my-internal-product
# some-private-service
# 111122223333
